WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.819 --> 00:00:11.849
Hi. Welcome back to the Wheel of Life
series...  online retreat, and today

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:25.760
we're going to do, for session six. I'm
sorry (laughs) we're going to do a meditation. And

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:31.439
during this online retreat we're
discussing three kinds--actually four

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:46.980
kinds--of meditation you can do to warm
up for your real meditation. And of course we did

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:54.300
the seven preparation steps already. Now
today we're going to do what's called

00:00:54.300 --> 00:01:06.270
"the eight technique meditations." And
these meditations help you improve your

00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:20.009
meditation technique. They're not
actually meditations themselves. It's

00:01:20.009 --> 00:01:25.110
like we are just building a stronger
microscope, but we're not looking at

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.369
anything with the microscope.

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:45.560
So these meditations are kind of
exciting. And kind of sexy. But, please,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:53.120
they are not real meditations. You are
just sharpening the knife; you are not

00:01:53.120 --> 00:02:04.790
cutting the fruit yet. Cutting the fruit is
real meditation. Sharpening the knife is

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:14.660
just improving your concentration. If you
want to say it a different way, you can

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:25.430
say these eight technique meditations
help you reach shamatha. And shamatha

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:34.520
means ... literally it means
"peacefulness," but it means the kind of

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:39.680
perfect focus you're going to have to
develop if you want to see emptiness

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:58.900
later. So personally, in my daily
meditation, I mix up different

00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:07.790
preliminaries. Some days I feel like
doing the seven preliminaries because

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:11.200
I'd like to start with my teacher.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:26.569
And that's a very powerful karma for
starting your meditation. But sometimes before

00:03:26.569 --> 00:03:37.100
meditation, I like to use these eight
technique meditations. Sometimes I want

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:41.590
to call them "getting quiet" meditations.

00:03:43.959 --> 00:03:55.610
And the goal of these eight is to get
quieter, and quieter, and quieter. And then

00:03:55.610 --> 00:04:04.790
you shift to the real meditation. So in
session six, today, we're just going to

00:04:04.790 --> 00:04:15.820
practice those eight "getting quieter
technique meditations," and then in

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:24.830
tomorrow's segment--session seven--I'll
show you how to use those eight to get

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:32.020
into your meditation, and then do a real
meditation.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:37.560
The picture that we use for these

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:45.380
eight is a picture of the sky and the
sea.

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:46.640
And you'll understand that more as

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:50.880
we go through these meditations.

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.360
These
are traditionally divided into two sets

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:57.960
of four and four.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:06.560
And the nickname for them
in Tibetan Buddhism is sam suk (BSAM GZUGS), sam

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:08.770
suk.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:15.080
sam (BSAM) is short for samten (BSAM GTAN),

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:21.960
and
samten, like dhyana in Sanskrit, and

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:27.620
the word chan or zen comes from that.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:36.660
So actually all meditations
are dhyana, but the first four are,

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:44.180
together, traditionally they are called
samten shi (BSAM GTAN BZHI)--"the four meditation levels."

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:57.980
And as you know if you studied the Lion's
Dance, these these are divided into

00:05:57.980 --> 00:06:02.990
cause meditations and result meditations.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:12.480
"Cause meditation" means if you do these
four samtens or dhyanas over and over

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:25.800
in this life--many, many, many times--when
you die, you could be born into what we

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:38.870
call the form realm. Form is also a
nickname, and it means the realm of

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:51.210
beings who look like superheroes. So in
that realm everybody looks like Iron Man,

00:06:51.210 --> 00:07:04.280
or Thor, or Wonder Woman. They have very, very beautiful
forms, so it's called form realm meditation.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:20.050
Then we go to the second set of four. So,
the whole eight are called sam suk. The

00:07:20.050 --> 00:07:24.280
sam (BSAM) means the samten--four kinds of
meditation to reach the form realm

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:42.970
rebirth of Thor and Iron Man. And to
call the second set suk (GZUGS) is very

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:58.470
confusing, because suk means "physical
form." But really those realms are suk-me (GZUGS MED)--

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:11.349
formless realms. And you are born without any
gross physical body there, if you do these four

00:08:11.349 --> 00:08:18.039
meditations. Whether you become poor or
whether you become a person who is just

00:08:18.039 --> 00:08:21.539
a brain and no body,

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:37.240
you are still in sansara, and there's a lot of
suffering there. So we don't do these

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:46.630
meditations to reach those two realms. We
use these meditations to get quieter, and

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:59.829
quieter, and quieter so we can do a
higher meditation. So when you say "we're trying to

00:08:59.829 --> 00:09:02.610
reach shamatha,"

00:09:03.510 --> 00:09:14.500
it doesn't mean peace in the sense of
Nirvana; it means peace in the sense of

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:27.010
perfect concentration. And perfect quiet.
So let's start. Take your meditation

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:34.570
position. Make sure you're comfortable--
don't start your meditation until you

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:45.460
are really comfortable. Stomach is a
little bit ... lower abdomen is a little bit

00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:54.150
pushed in. The perfect way to do that,

00:09:55.590 --> 00:10:08.290
when you exhale, then push a little extra
air out, and that will also prevent problems

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:22.570
with too much prana build-up. Shoulders
back, chest out, the hands come back on

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:40.660
the legs a little bit. Face is calm. Many of
us, when we concentrate, we scowl. So try

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:51.010
to concentrate without scowling. I like
to play music. When I play sitar, for

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:53.910
example, I scowl

00:10:56.580 --> 00:11:07.770
because I'm concentrating. So during
meditation, especially these eight, try to

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:22.230
concentrate but don't scowl. The face
is very pleasant, relaxed, little smile.

00:11:23.220 --> 00:11:31.380
Now usually we start a meditation by
watching our breath for about ten breaths.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:44.650
But it's traditional--especially in the
"Lion's Dance"--to start this meditation in

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:57.040
a completely different way. So before you
start the eight, we're going to listen to

00:11:57.040 --> 00:12:12.610
any subtle sounds in this room. It might
be the sound of a few cars outside, it

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:17.670
might be the sound of some family
members in your apartment.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:29.980
The sound of a refrigerator is very
typical in most houses. In this room

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:34.790
right now,
at the Sedona College of International

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:43.210
Management and the headquarters of ACI,

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:48.580
we have air conditioning going right now.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:59.360
So whatever sound you have available in
your place, please put your mind on that

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:12.110
sound. I enjoy the image of putting my
head on a pillow. When I put my head on

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:23.090
my pillow at night, I so enjoy that
moment. And the head goes down to the

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:31.100
pillow and it stays there. You don't
raise your head, put it back, raise your

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:39.620
head, put it back, raise your head ...
you don't do that. So for this sound

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:51.290
meditation before we do the eight technique
meditations, please relax your mind on

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:55.850
that sound in your room like you are
putting your head on a pillow and leave

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:58.240
it there.

00:14:06.079 --> 00:14:20.370
Here we go. Stanley and I will put our
minds on the air conditioning. Again, personally

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:30.720
I like to time the parts of my
meditation. I might do ten breaths on each

00:14:30.720 --> 00:14:43.199
part or twenty. People ask me, "Isn't that a
distraction, when you think about your

00:14:43.199 --> 00:14:57.329
breath when you're supposed to be thinking
about the air conditioner?" But if you

00:14:57.329 --> 00:15:07.920
practice meditation every day, the ten
breaths becomes natural to you, and it

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.939
won't be a distraction. Okay, here we go.

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:04.540
Try to keep your mind on the sound.

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:07.589
Now we're going to go into the first of
the eight technique meditations. And

00:17:07.589 --> 00:17:13.070
please put your mind on your heartbeat.

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:23.400
For me, it feels like I'm in my head and
I'm kind of feeling my heart beat in

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:45.840
my chest. And I'm not inside the heart,
I'm just observing the heart. If you meditate

00:17:45.840 --> 00:17:52.350
a lot and if you have a quiet place to
meditate, you can follow your heartbeat--

00:17:52.350 --> 00:18:08.700
the pulse--in your ears. So here we
go.

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:20.340
Relax. Don't rush. Just have fun.
Please remember to push the breath out

00:18:20.340 --> 00:18:39.990
at the exhale--at the end of the exhale, until your
lower abdomen tightens, very slightly--all

00:18:39.990 --> 00:18:47.850
throughout these meditations. OK. Let's
focus on our heartbeats, and try not to

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:57.980
think of other things. These eight
meditations are described as dropping

00:18:57.980 --> 00:19:11.850
the last level and moving up to the next
level. Each level is more quiet than the last

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:24.210
level--higher, higher quiet. So you almost
consciously say, "I'm going to

00:19:24.210 --> 00:19:28.740
stop listening to the air conditioner
and I'm going to move up to a quieter

00:19:28.740 --> 00:19:31.790
heartbeat."

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:45.980
So try to stay on the heartbeat and try
not to listen to the air-conditioner

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:57.820
anymore. You should feel like you're
getting quieter and quieter.

00:21:51.680 --> 00:22:00.260
Now we're going to go even more
quiet--the second of the eight technique

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:14.860
meditations. Let's go inside our heart. We
will still be listening to the heartbeat,

00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:21.950
but it will feel like the walls of our
little meditation room are beating

00:22:21.950 --> 00:22:25.180
because we're inside the heart.

00:22:36.210 --> 00:22:52.050
Now the inside of the heart is kind of
wet and gooey, but for this meditation

00:22:52.230 --> 00:23:00.000
you have to imagine that inside the
heart is a lovely, elegant meditation room.

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:15.580
Sunlight is coming through the windows.
You have a very comfortable meditation

00:23:15.580 --> 00:23:26.400
seat. It's super quiet, but the walls
around you--the heart walls--are beating.

00:23:30.059 --> 00:23:42.820
So now drop down from your head and
enter your heart. And let's stay in that

00:23:42.820 --> 00:23:52.050
more quiet place with the heart beating
around us.

00:25:02.070 --> 00:25:07.590
Now we'll go to the third technique
meditation, the third part of the form

00:25:07.590 --> 00:25:21.240
realm meditation. And imagine there's a
meditation room at the center of your

00:25:21.240 --> 00:25:32.610
meditation room. I like to think of it like a
very expensive apartment on the top of a

00:25:32.610 --> 00:25:50.460
tall apartment building. And all the
windows are glass, and there's a room at

00:25:50.460 --> 00:26:02.240
the center of the apartment. And I go
into that room and I close the door.

00:26:02.240 --> 00:26:10.170
There's still some sunlight coming in
and it's still a beautiful, elegant room

00:26:10.170 --> 00:26:25.890
with good air, but the heart beating in
the walls, now it sounds very far away--

00:26:25.890 --> 00:26:36.330
very faint. Okay, here we go to the
meditation room at the center of the

00:26:36.330 --> 00:26:38.540
heart.

00:26:42.539 --> 00:26:46.049
Even more quiet.

00:27:50.050 --> 00:27:59.590
Now I'd like you to imagine a small
table at your side--inside this inner

00:27:59.590 --> 00:28:13.870
room of the heart. And sitting on that
table is a small pot of sugar--white

00:28:13.870 --> 00:28:27.010
sugar. And you lift off the lid of the
sugar pot, and with the third finger of

00:28:27.010 --> 00:28:44.160
your left hand, you just touch the sugar,
slightly. And you lift the finger out and

00:28:44.250 --> 00:28:55.330
there's a few grains of sugar on the tip
of your finger. Focus on one of those grains of

00:28:55.330 --> 00:29:05.679
sugar, and then think to yourself, "Oh, I
would like to be inside that sugar

00:29:05.679 --> 00:29:17.620
crystal." It's super quiet. It's also super
anonymous--who's going to find you in the

00:29:17.620 --> 00:29:21.420
whole room inside a sugar crystal?

00:29:28.049 --> 00:29:35.760
In the whole world, in the whole universe,
it's a tiny, tiny, tiny, tiny, little place.

00:29:39.390 --> 00:29:45.929
"If I go inside there, I'll be super quiet.

00:29:49.080 --> 00:29:58.600
No one would ever find me there." So
imagine you are opening a door into the

00:29:58.600 --> 00:30:07.659
sugar crystal and you
kind of squeeze your mind through that

00:30:07.659 --> 00:30:18.400
little door. Then you're very surprised.
Inside it's a third meditation

00:30:18.400 --> 00:30:32.620
room--kind of large and very
comfortable. Light is coming in through

00:30:32.620 --> 00:30:46.960
the edges of the crystal, and you sit
down and meditate inside there. If

00:30:46.960 --> 00:30:52.929
someone came into your main meditation
room at this moment, in your

00:30:52.929 --> 00:30:55.140
house,

00:30:59.720 --> 00:31:04.350
how could they ever bother you? You are
in a single ... it's like you're

00:31:04.350 --> 00:31:21.720
in a single atom in a huge room. So let's
go inside and meditate. Very, very quiet

00:31:21.720 --> 00:31:25.640
inside--no more heartbeat at all.

00:32:24.290 --> 00:32:37.370
Now let's take a challenge. In the fifth of
the eight technique meditations, which is

00:32:37.370 --> 00:32:48.710
the first of the formless realm
meditations, we take a challenge. Can you

00:32:48.710 --> 00:33:00.680
fit the whole Pacific Ocean inside of
that sugar crystal? So now you

00:33:00.680 --> 00:33:12.830
become the Pacific Ocean. You are
thousands of miles wide. You're a few

00:33:12.830 --> 00:33:26.480
miles deep. You cover a good part of the
whole world. And Pacific Ocean--"pacific" means

00:33:26.480 --> 00:33:38.950
"peaceful." So you are this deep, peaceful,
blue ocean.

00:33:42.960 --> 00:33:46.320
Totally silent.

00:34:48.250 --> 00:34:53.669
Let's go even bigger and broader.

00:34:56.430 --> 00:35:10.060
Let's add the whole blue sky to the blue
water. This is the picture we used for

00:35:10.060 --> 00:35:18.390
this meditation. "I am the entire blue sky.

00:35:18.720 --> 00:35:25.200
And I am the entire blue Pacific Ocean. I

00:35:26.609 --> 00:35:38.280
stretch from the bottom of the ocean to
the top of the sky." Totally peaceful.

00:35:38.280 --> 00:35:41.520
Totally calm.

00:36:28.210 --> 00:36:32.250
What could be more quiet than that?

00:36:34.019 --> 00:36:48.339
"What if I just turned my whole mind off,
like a light?" It's actually ... technically,

00:36:48.339 --> 00:37:00.719
it's not possible--but let's pretend. "I'm
going to turn my mind off like a light and

00:37:02.400 --> 00:37:18.940
this will be more quiet than anything
before--like completely unconscious." Watch

00:37:18.940 --> 00:37:32.890
your mind. Keep it super quiet--no talking
in the mind at all. If a thought comes

00:37:32.890 --> 00:37:46.269
through, if some random image comes
through, if some interruption from the

00:37:46.269 --> 00:38:01.109
outside comes into the mind, go to
it and block it. Tell it to shut up.

00:38:01.109 --> 00:38:07.440
Push it out of the mind. Here we go.

00:38:55.080 --> 00:39:03.720
Now we're going to go to meditation
level eight--the highest level of the

00:39:03.720 --> 00:39:08.490
formless realm meditations, which lead
you to the formless realm if you do them

00:39:08.490 --> 00:39:25.740
a lot in this life. "Now I'm also going to
shut up the part of my mind which is

00:39:25.740 --> 00:39:31.310
watching my mind to see if my mind is
thinking about anything."

00:39:38.390 --> 00:39:51.000
"Now if random thoughts or ideas come through
my mind, no one will be there to hear

00:39:51.000 --> 00:39:59.840
them," which is a deeper quiet place.

00:40:00.920 --> 00:40:07.760
Nobody even watching. Let's try.

00:41:02.470 --> 00:41:14.859
Now let's dedicate the meditation--these
eight technique meditations--just with a wish

00:41:14.859 --> 00:41:19.960
in your heart that all the people
in the world would find this kind of

00:41:19.960 --> 00:41:22.710
peace and quiet.

00:41:45.420 --> 00:41:58.170
Slowly open your eyes. Take a stretch. See
you tomorrow in the next session.

